[{:db/id "q-49308/selection/4c919dd28b6dc49158e4bc0cd4ecb2267c6fa1a0cbd5673af1ca376ab1c8a23e" :answer/id #uuid "ec92d1cb-40e5-5ba8-a10b-e0f065531685" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49308/selection/928fbd2c85ef2222ec96ebd82b2eb0375907dd122d9c9dc6aad18e7ba8be00b1" :answer/id #uuid "22bbf7fd-2cbe-55e0-9408-f3e829be27e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49308/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "851dcf61-831e-5b7c-9f8a-2db913b12bd3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49308/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" :answer/id #uuid "9c5699c0-de88-537a-9311-86197a3b5ceb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49308/selection/7731c9af51b2c33d92792f2597c202100294f6851d8e1d7a2508f8fc3f5f1dd1" :answer/id #uuid "78faa54b-32fd-52b3-a23a-c9b6a516ede1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49308/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8e0a427b-01a7-5e48-85b4-c36e85edbaba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-49308/selection/928fbd2c85ef2222ec96ebd82b2eb0375907dd122d9c9dc6aad18e7ba8be00b1" :answer-field/choices ["q-49308/selection/4c919dd28b6dc49158e4bc0cd4ecb2267c6fa1a0cbd5673af1ca376ab1c8a23e" "q-49308/selection/928fbd2c85ef2222ec96ebd82b2eb0375907dd122d9c9dc6aad18e7ba8be00b1" "q-49308/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" "q-49308/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" "q-49308/selection/7731c9af51b2c33d92792f2597c202100294f6851d8e1d7a2508f8fc3f5f1dd1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-49308" :question/id #uuid "d89bb6ec-58ba-5dce-8d06-89f659d78ac4" :question/math-academy-id "q-49308" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068772/assets/288b3eeaf1168316f2d8f43fa9484032daa8c9006a1c8355b8edfd1186dc2add.png)\n\nThe graph of a function $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Given $g(t)={\\int }_{-4}^{t}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x,$ determine the value of $g(2).$" :question/worked-solution "Evaluating $g(t)$ at $t=2,$ we get the following definite integral:\n\n$$\ng(2)={\\int }_{-4}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nThis integral gives the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068772/assets/9f570d7f04bcf5645a97a6a1d85e72f602c436ef184e841fc4c998c0d5eb8e2e.png)\n\nNote that the graph above consists of $2$ parts:\n\n- $x\\in [-4,-1],$ for which the region between the curve and the $x$-axis is a rectangle. This corresponds to the area ${A}_{1}.$\n\n- $x\\in [-1,2],$ for which the region between the curve and the $x$-axis is a trapezoid. This corresponds to the area ${A}_{2}.$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as follows:\n\n$$\ng(2)={\\int }_{-4}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-4}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{-1}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute these integrals:\n\n- To find the first integral where $x\\in [-4,-1],$ we compute the area ${A}_{1}$ of the rectangle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To find the second integral where $x\\in [-1,2],$ we compute the area ${A}_{2}$ of the trapezoid as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot (1+2) \\\\  & =4.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(2) & ={\\int }_{-4}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={A}_{1}+{A}_{2}=6+4.5=10.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-49308/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "639c3818-9c51-5dc5-abd5-c833fec45ac1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-49308"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-49309"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068772/assets/af84278943fcf2d9c4e3b99c115a4d82672fe50f2bfed8be7be84648985f80df.png)\n\nThe graph of a function $y=f(x)$ is shown above. It consists of two lines and the arc of a semi-circle of radius $2.$ Given $g(t)={\\int }_{-3}^{t}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x,$ determine the value of $g(3).$" :question/worked-solution "Evaluating $g(t)$ at $t=3,$ we get the following definite integral:\n\n$$\ng(3)={\\int }_{-3}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nThis integral gives the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068772/assets/4d1f408db7fcb99092f7e61afc4c0a25501d3349790e54983f481408c58f9951.png)\n\nNote that the graph above consists of $2$ parts:\n\n- $x\\in [-3,1],$ for which the region between the curve and the $x$-axis is a semi-circle and a rectangle below it. This corresponds to the area ${A}_{1}.$\n\n- $x\\in [1,3],$ for which the region between the curve and the $x$-axis is a trapezoid. This corresponds to the area ${A}_{2}.$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as follows:\n\n$$\ng(3)={\\int }_{-3}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-3}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute these integrals:\n\n- To find the first integral where $x\\in [-3,1],$ we compute the area ${A}_{1}$ of the semi-circle and the rectangle below it as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi {r}^{2}+bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi \\cdot {2}^{2}+4\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2\\pi +4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To find the second integral where $x\\in [1,3],$ we compute the area ${A}_{2}$ of the trapezoid as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}h(a+b) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot (1+3) \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(3) & ={\\int }_{-3}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={A}_{1}+{A}_{2}=(2\\pi +4)+4=2\\pi +8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-103778/selection/609ddefa393fd0c8e63f6085f385ac632723b91519d54d30cdcfb24fb3257f0a" :answer/id #uuid "cd98d233-50ae-538f-9ab1-03b1028a79b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A(t)=\\frac{5}{6}t+\\frac{11{t}^{2}}{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103778/selection/f7899239f6c449752a307a010b53836ccbc65a60299f8c9b3514ab0f93dcb6c9" :answer/id #uuid "73d19e40-ba02-5c7b-a452-b6944ddfaffd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A(t)=5+\\frac{11{t}^{2}}{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103778/selection/a0a1f6206b9628c19964d08f26c422b55a621d0752b800a2f8fb4c199fbef4be" :answer/id #uuid "a528bb8b-4f94-5c25-b4b3-b722bb5f74ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A(t)=5+\\frac{5}{6}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103778/selection/908856318cc7c4533e9471b932faace5ab07ed45eaffbf355c75724362c8ad9d" :answer/id #uuid "7a341548-1213-5609-9861-3793f4607179" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A(t)=\\frac{11{t}^{2}}{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103778/selection/da761a4b9c0d4f0989d016f3e3ab3dcd88403eb9f6bae428927c667969c945a7" :answer/id #uuid "a58e441a-b64b-5736-8941-bf99e46494f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A(t)=5+\\frac{5}{6}t+\\frac{11{t}^{2}}{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103778/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "41cf300e-79d9-5b26-9829-c540109921a4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-103778/selection/908856318cc7c4533e9471b932faace5ab07ed45eaffbf355c75724362c8ad9d" :answer-field/choices ["q-103778/selection/609ddefa393fd0c8e63f6085f385ac632723b91519d54d30cdcfb24fb3257f0a" "q-103778/selection/f7899239f6c449752a307a010b53836ccbc65a60299f8c9b3514ab0f93dcb6c9" "q-103778/selection/a0a1f6206b9628c19964d08f26c422b55a621d0752b800a2f8fb4c199fbef4be" "q-103778/selection/908856318cc7c4533e9471b932faace5ab07ed45eaffbf355c75724362c8ad9d" "q-103778/selection/da761a4b9c0d4f0989d016f3e3ab3dcd88403eb9f6bae428927c667969c945a7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-103778" :question/id #uuid "470653e9-5d5b-542e-9020-2a9f1d9e16a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-103778" :question/problem "A gas station pump dispenses gas into an empty gas tank at a rate of $\\frac{11}{6}t$ liters per second. Write an expression for $A(t),$ the total volume of gas in the tank at time $t,$ where $t$ is the time measured in second." :question/worked-solution "Let $f(t)=\\frac{11}{6}t$ be the rate at which the gas pump dispenses gas, and let $A(T)$ be the total number of liters in the car after $T$ seconds.\n\nUsing our formula for the accumulation of change, we have\n\n$$\nA(T)=A(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{T}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the known information and carrying out the necessary integration gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A(T) & =A(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{T}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =0+{\\int }_{0}^{T}\\frac{11}{6}t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={(\\frac{11}{6}\\cdot \\frac{{t}^{2}}{2})|}_{0}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{11{T}^{2}}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, let's rewrite our final answer in terms of the original variable $t.$ We have\n\n$$\nA(t)=\\frac{11{t}^{2}}{12}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-103778/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9a8be4bb-bbfe-5a5d-872c-91b4d67edc2f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-103778"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-346534/field-1/f345fac9a81ccd096b9959c6e7a966a446e93e73b82d111a376f9064132509fd" :answer/id #uuid "e7284f24-a13a-5561-8590-3d350cff79e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346534/field-1/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" :answer/id #uuid "f95ca8be-e73e-5244-a320-018dd4061aa5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346534/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "66c993e2-b41f-5743-b634-4b00f2295784" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-346534/field-1/f345fac9a81ccd096b9959c6e7a966a446e93e73b82d111a376f9064132509fd" :answer-field/choices ["q-346534/field-1/f345fac9a81ccd096b9959c6e7a966a446e93e73b82d111a376f9064132509fd" "q-346534/field-1/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-346534" :question/id #uuid "9e6fc43c-b4e2-588d-9575-ad3c07d6f70b" :question/math-academy-id "q-346534" :question/problem "Calculate $F(9)$ where $F(x)={\\int }_{1}^{x}\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{t}}\\,\\text{d}t.$\n\n$F(9)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Evaluating $F(x)$ at $x=9,$ we get the following definite integral:\n\n$$\nF\\,(9)={\\int }_{1}^{9}\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{t}}\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nThen, computing the definite integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(9) & ={\\int }_{1}^{9}\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{t}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =6{\\int }_{1}^{9}{t}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =12{t}^{1/2}\\,{|}_{1}^{9} \\\\  & =12({9}^{1/2}-{1}^{1/2}) \\\\  & =12(3-1) \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-346534/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3945f55a-2d0a-5515-801b-55af29af24d9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-346534"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
